sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (Nick 2026-11-07): stage 2 of the command development pipeline. A task VM, where an agent or Nick develops a command and the proof cases run too, is a fixed slot `<node>-tvm-<n>` from the host's image. The image holds everything installed and ready: orbit-agent, the Pi server, the tools, Swamp, sshd and UFW, a warm checkout of main with `vendor/` and `node_modules/`, and the nested fleet (a Gateway with Swamp, an app-dev Node, an app-prod Node) as Incus system containers, migrated and running, with a `base` snapshot each. The containers mount the outer VM's checkout as a disk device, so an edit reaches them at once. A claim only starts the slot: docs/cli/tasks/provision.mmd.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 2 · development environment
  %% kind: pipeline.2-development-environment
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=slot tone=purple
  %% lane NT icon=server pill=fleet tone=gray
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>provision run
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant VM as Slot<br/>outer · operator
  participant NT as Nested fleet<br/>3 containers
  Note over GW: Claim a free slot<br/>group at a commit
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - an external task group in `todo` and a free slot on a host, enrolled from the host's promoted image
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the group holds the slot; its Node, WireGuard peer, agent secret, Pi token, host key and workspace Instance already exist, so nothing is minted or published
  %%> - a proof is placed only on a host whose promoted image holds every change of what the image carries, up to the merge base of the proof commit with main (`TaskVmImageInputs`); otherwise the admission answers `tasks.capacity_unavailable` and names the release the host's image comes from
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>tasks provision
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the same run for a person, an agent or a CI proof
  SW->>H: Start the slot<br/>incus start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts the stopped slot; about 7 s to the guest agent
  SW->>VM: Fetch the task branch<br/>onto the warm checkout
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `git fetch` of the group's branch with an App read token minted for this step, then checkout; the token never stays on the VM
  %%> - `composer install` or `npm ci` only when a lock file differs from main's
  %%> - no step brings the task branch up to date with main: `tasks:sync` fetches refs only and the author merges, as stage 4 asks for a conflict
  SW->>NT: Start the containers<br/>from base
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - restores `base` and starts the Gateway with Swamp, app-dev and app-prod; 3.5 to 7 s each
  %%> - migrations run only when the branch adds new ones
  %%> - the outer VM is the operator of the nested fleet; that operator key belongs to the nested network only, is private to each VM's fleet and is baked with the fleet, so it is no part of the slot's identity
  SW->>VM: Check ready<br/>one exec
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one exec checks the agent, Pi, the tunnel and the three containers; Swamp's `assert` decides
  SW-->>GW: Environment ready<br/>terminal event
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the group runs on the slot; the proof (stage 3) or the proof CI (stage 4) uses the fleet
  %%> - target under 30 s from admission
  loop while the author develops
    VM->>NT: Edit, test, call the CLI<br/>the checkout is shared
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the author edits and runs tests on the outer VM; PHP in the nested containers sees the change on the next request
    %%> - the candidate CLI on the outer VM talks to the nested Gateway as the operator
    %%> - after a new migration, the author runs the migrations in the nested Gateway
  end
  opt the author wants a clean fleet
    SW->>NT: Restore the base snapshot<br/>a reboot · 5–16 s
    %%> What it keeps:
    %%> - the outer VM, Pi and the checkout
  end
  SW->>H: Release the slot<br/>stop · roll back to clean
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - at the end of the group, the slot stops and rolls back to its `clean` snapshot (docs/cli/tasks/vm-slot-release.mmd); its identity stays
